lines=['# Episode10 — The Party Cake Went to the Wrong House!','', '> **Format:**80 continuous story shots ×15seconds = **20:00 story runtime**.','> **Status:**authored story and still-image preproduction draft. No performed voices or generated video; creator visual approval and individual motion first frames pending.','> **Story-only:**natural General American family conversation; no viewer drills, quiz, recap narrator or timed practice. Optional creator-authored practice belongs after the story.','', 'Following the garden episode, the family celebrates a weekend of helping each other. A prepaid cake is marked delivered, but the photo shows a green door. Dan’s confidence gives way to uncertainty; everyone contributes observations, asks politely, and checks the actual order before recovering one safely chilled cake. The warm finale recalls earlier adventures without turning into a lesson recap.','', '## Arc','', '-001–016:prepare a modest six-person party; Aunt Rose stops briefly and leaves.','-017–032:notice missing cake, test assumptions, compare order and photograph, contact delivery support.','-033–048:walk together along the same sidewalk, identify18, ring once and ask with facts.','-049–060:verify order/label/cold storage/seal; thank neighbor, return and refrigerate.','-061–072:resolve support request, wash hands, serve six slices in fixed seats.','-073–080:brief audio hello from Ed, family celebration and earned emotional ending.','', '## Timing, identity and geography','', 'Actions, waiting, food handling and eating include explicitly marked story-time ellipses where needed;15seconds is an editorial slot, not a provider-duration guarantee. Original W01 actors/home remain fixed. Rose’s new reference is the provisional draft shared with Episode04, not an approved redesign. Ed never appears onscreen; the neighbor has no face. Dialogue in the Off-screen cast field is audible without inserting an onscreen actor.','', 'Exact address/phone/checklist text uses editorial SVGs. All addresses, delivery messages and times are fictional props. Detailed props, cameo, evidence, food and serving state are in [CONTINUITY.md](CONTINUITY.md).','', '## Timed story shots','']
